Mutation proof: tools/nova_trust.py, top-level `bootchain` optionality
=========================================================================

Date: 2026-10-02
Track: C2 manifest format (tools/nova_trust.py, tests/test_trust.py)
Base commit: 65e0270 "K4b evidence: mutation-kill transcript (weakened phnum
              check, fixture drift) + 13-stage check log"

The finding
-----------
docs/manifest-format.md:116 calls bootchain "An optional `bootchain` object",
tools/nova_trust.py build_manifest() only emits it when the caller passes one,
and every bootchain content check in structure_errors() is already guarded by
`if "bootchain" in m`. But _TOP (line 254) includes "bootchain", and
top_required was built as `_TOP | {"signature"}`, which made bootchain MANDATORY
at the top level. Since df69025 that meant every bootchain-less manifest was
structurally invalid, and 15 of the 24 tests in tests/test_trust.py failed.

This log records the mutation that proves the fix is load-bearing.

The fix
-------
tools/nova_trust.py, ~lines 287-293:

    # bootchain is optional at the top level: docs/manifest-format.md calls
    # it "An optional bootchain object", build_manifest() only emits it when
    # given, and every content check below is already 'if "bootchain" in m'.
    # Requiring it here made every bootchain-less manifest structurally
    # invalid since df69025.
    top_required = (_TOP - {"bootchain"}) | ({"signature"} if require_signature else set())
    top_optional = {"bootchain"} | (set() if require_signature else {"signature"})

Transcript
----------
Shell is Git Bash on Windows; `py -3` is the interpreter.

$ mkdir -p build && cp tools/nova_trust.py build/nova_trust.fixed.bak && cmp tools/nova_trust.py build/nova_trust.fixed.bak && echo BACKUP_OK
BACKUP_OK

MUTATION: revert the two lines above to the df69025 behaviour, i.e. require
bootchain again and drop it from the optional set:

    top_required = _TOP | ({"signature"} if require_signature else set())
    top_optional = set() if require_signature else {"signature"}

$ py -3 tests/test_trust.py 2>&1 | tail -4
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Ran 24 tests in 5.824s

FAILED (failures=3, errors=12)

So the fix is load-bearing: re-requiring bootchain kills 15 of 24 tests. This
is the same signature as the pre-fix suite, so the mutation reproduces the
original bug exactly rather than a different one.

RESTORE, from the byte-identical backup (not `git checkout --`, because the fix
was uncommitted at the time of the mutation):

$ cp build/nova_trust.fixed.bak tools/nova_trust.py; cmp build/nova_trust.fixed.bak tools/nova_trust.py && echo RESTORE_IDENTICAL
RESTORE_IDENTICAL

$ py -3 tests/test_trust.py 2>&1 | tail -4
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Ran 24 tests in 10.323s

OK

Scope note: this log covers the top-level optionality only. Whether
bootchain's own members are required is a separate question, answered in
docs/logs/manifest-schema-drift.log.